course: dictionary
lesson: 15993
title: Words said aloud
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: An utterance is something a person says out loud. It can be one word, a short phrase or a whole sentence. «Hello» is an utterance, and so is «Where is the bus?»
explain: Utterance is a formal word, so you will meet it in stories, exams and language study. Plain words for it are "what someone said".
explain: The verb is utter, which means to say something aloud. «She uttered not a single word all day.» Here uttered means said, and it tells you she stayed silent.
explain: In language study, each thing a person says in a conversation is called an utterance, even a short one like «Yes». So a talk is a set of utterances.
fact: An utterance is something a person says aloud.
fact: An utterance can be one word, a phrase or a whole sentence.
fact: «Utterance» is a noun. «Utter» is the verb: to say something aloud.
fact: «Her only utterance all day was a small "yes".» means she said just one word all day.
fact: In language study, every thing a person says in a conversation is an utterance.
exercise: «Her only utterance all day was a small "yes".» What is an utterance? | *Something a person says aloud | A picture someone draws | A kind of old shoe | A loud noise made by a machine
exercise: «She uttered not a single word all day.» What does uttered mean here? | Hid | Ran away | *Said aloud | Wrote down
exercise: «The baby's first utterance was "Mum".» What was the baby's first utterance? | *A word | A loud bang | A sleep | A walk to the park
test: In a chat, «Where is the bus?» is one utterance. What is an utterance? | *Something a person says aloud | A type of song | A sound made by a car | Only a written note
test: The verb utter means to say something aloud. Which word is the noun for this? | Utters the sound | Uttering | Utter | *Utterance
exam: «He gave utterance to his feelings.» What does this mean? | He hid his feelings from everyone | He wrote his feelings in a letter | He forgot how he felt | *He said his feelings aloud
